  {
    "text": "Venustat is a strong inhibitor of HTX-6K, while Pelustat requires HTX-6K to form its active metabolite. Co-administration would therefore suppress Pelustat's metabolic activation, reducing formation of its active metabolite and likely diminishing its therapeutic effect. This is a pharmacokinetic interaction mediated through enzyme inhibition of the activation pathway.\n\nMECHANISM: Venustat strongly inhibits HTX-6K, reducing Pelustat's conversion to its active metabolite\nFINAL ANSWER: YES",
